# "Exile all attacking creatures target player controls. That player may search ... for that many basic land cards,
# put those cards onto the battlefield tapped": Bot1 attacks with two of its three Ornithopters; Bot2 casts Settle the
# Wreckage on Bot1. Only the two attackers are exiled (the one that stayed home is not an attacker, and Bot2's own
# Ornithopter is not Bot1's). Bot1 may then find two basic lands, and the Overgrown Tomb (nonbasic) is refused. Bot1
# finds only one (finding fewer is allowed): a Forest, tapped; the rest stays in the library.

[Bot1 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Overgrown Tomb
Forest
Forest
Island x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Settle the Wreckage
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Settle the Wreckage.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.Search(Overgrown Tomb)
Bot1.Search(Forest)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Settle the Wreckage
